        "text": "Questions\n1.\nExplain how the CWD model enhances the efficiency of multi-agent systems, using the travel\nplanning system as an example.\n2.\nWhat is the significance of \u201crole\u201d and \u201cbackstory\u201d in LLM agent design, and how do they\ncontribute to system prompts? Provide an example.\n3.\nCompare and contrast the core travel workers with analysis and intelligence workers in the\ntravel planning system. How do their functions complement each other?\n4.\nDescribe the key aspects of communication and collaboration in a CWD-based system, including\nprotocols, coordination mechanisms, and knowledge sharing.\n5.\nHow does instruction formatting contribute to effective agent communication in an LLM-based\nsystem? Explain with examples of input and output structures.\nExploring the Coordinator, Worker, and Delegator Approach\n158",
